    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_signed_packet_section_vanishing",
    "title": "A=1 core-one signed packets have no degree-two section",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "bounded nilpotent modification and ordinary-point removal",
    "statement": "In every core-one degree-one packet with ordinary heavy incidences, the positive part of the exact signed divisor is a proper subdivisor of the distinguished vertical fibre, of degree r=3 in the first two packets and r=4 in the last. Its pushforward has splitting O plus O(1-d)^r plus O(-d)^(e-1-r) and only its canonical section. The disjoint nonempty ordinary divisor removes that section, so h^0(C,O_C(rho+2,-e-1))=0 in all three signed packets.",
